  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mt-12 mb-6 dark:text-on-primary">Interesting Facts</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-body dark:text-muted">
    <li>Provisional tax is an advance payment system that allows taxpayers to spread their tax burden across the year rather than paying a lump sum at year-end.</li>
    <li>Provisional tax payments are split into two equal installments, typically due in November and April of the relevant year.</li>
    <li>If provisional tax exceeds your final tax liability, the IRD automatically refunds the difference after assessment.</li>
    <li>The IRD may waive or reduce provisional tax if you can prove your income will drop significantly, such as due to retirement or business closure.</li>
    <li>Late payment attracts an initial 5% surcharge, followed by an additional 10% surcharge if the tax remains unpaid after six months.</li>
  </ul>

